{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123658","id":4584932263,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEUiDpw","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123658","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123658.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123658.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123658","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123658/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123658/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123658/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/5017b3b63302c0e99497a93bd468f019401668bf","number":123658,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Fix deferred editor documentation callbacks running after cleanup","user":{"login":"blueloveTH","id":28104173,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4MTA0MTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28104173?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueloveTH","html_url":"https://github.com/blueloveTH","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueloveTH/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueloveTH/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueloveTH/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueloveTH/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueloveTH/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueloveTH/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueloveTH/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueloveTH/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueloveTH/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #111645 \r\n- Closes #111048 \r\n\r\nThe editor may crash when a project loads a GDExtension that registers a class and exits shortly after the initial import (coldstart; no `.godot` directory). This can occur during automated tests that launch the editor with `--headless`. The existing discussions have already identified the root cause and several possible fixes. This PR implements the approach I tested and found to work best.\r\n\r\n`EditorHelp::cleanup_doc()` waits for the worker thread to finish, but that thread may have queued callbacks for the main thread. After `cleanup_doc()` deletes the documentation data and sets `doc` to nullptr, a queued callback such as `_gen_extensions_docs()` may execute and dereference the now-null `doc` pointer.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nThis PR binds deferred callbacks to an owner object tied to `doc`, so pending callbacks are skipped after cleanup automatically. I am using [skyostil’s MRE](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111645#issuecomment-3405677801), master crashed in all 3 runs, while the fixed branch exited successfully in all 3 runs.\r\n\r\n### Existing suggestions\r\n\r\n| Suggestion | Assessment |\r\n| --- | --- |\r\n| [Skyostil: guard `_gen_extensions_docs()` against null `doc`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111645) | Prevents the reported crash, but leaves other deferred callbacks unprotected. |\r\n| [Jojo-1000: check `doc` in every main-thread callback](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111048#issuecomment-3363475937) | Requires per-callback checks and cannot distinguish stale callbacks if `doc` is recreated. |\r\n| [Calinou: delay shutdown with `--quit-after` or `--frame-delay`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111048) | It is a workaround. |\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archiv